# Penetration Test Report — Harbour / HIX Web Application

**Project:** Customer Management Web Service (Harbour + HIX Framework)  
**Date:** 2026-01-01  
**Auditor:** AI Penetration Test Agent  
**Scope:** All source code, configuration, routes, and views in `/home/jack/Projects/pi-agent/webapp/`  
**Reference:** OWASP Top 10 2021 · OWASP API Security Top 10 2023  

---

## Executive Summary

A systematic review of the Harbour/HIX Customer Management application identified **12 security findings** across the following categories:

| Severity | Count |
|----------|-------|
| 🔴 Critical | 2 |
| 🟠 High | 3 |
| 🟡 Medium | 5 |
| 🟢 Low | 2 |

The most critical issues are **plaintext hardcoded credentials** in the user model and **missing CSRF protection on the login endpoint** (which paradoxically has rate-limiting). Several medium-severity issues around information disclosure, session configuration, and input sanitization should be addressed before production deployment.

