### C4 — Debug/Information Disclosure in Main Page

- **Vulnerability Name & CWE ID:** Information Exposure Through Unnecessary Data — CWE-200
- **Severity Rating:** 🟠 **High**
- **Technical Explanation:**  
  The main page (`www/views/main.html`) displays **verbose internal security information** to authenticated users:
  ```html
  <table class="table table-striped">
     <tr><td>ID</td><td>{{ hb_HGetDef( hUser, 'id', '?' ) }}</td></tr>
     <tr><td>Name</td><td>{{ cName }}</td></tr>
     <tr><td>Roles</td><td>{{ cRoles }}</td></tr>
  </table>

  <br><strong>Authorization roles for user: {{ UAuthUser('name','?') }}</strong>
  <br>UHasRole('customers'):          {{ if( UHasRole( 'customers'           ), 'Yes', 'No' ) }}
  <br>UHasRole('customers', 'show'):  {{ if( UHasRole( 'customers', 'show'   ), 'Yes', 'No' ) }}
  <br>UHasRole('customers', 'edit'):  {{ if( UHasRole( 'customers', 'edit'   ), 'Yes', 'No' ) }}
  <br>UHasRole('customers', 'create'):{{ if( UHasRole( 'customers', 'create' ), 'Yes', 'No' ) }}
  <br>UHasRole('customers', 'delete'):{{ if( UHasRole( 'customers', 'delete' ), 'Yes', 'No' ) }}
  <br>UHasRole('customers', 'xxx'):   {{ if( UHasRole( 'customers', 'xxx'    ), 'Yes', 'No' ) }}
  ```

  This exposes:
  1. The user's internal ID
  2. The complete role list
  3. **Every possible scope/action** the application checks (`customers:show`, `customers:edit`, `customers:create`, `customers:delete`, `xxx`)
  4. The presence of a `dummy` role check
  5. The internal API function names (`UAuthUser`, `UHasRole`)

  An attacker who gains access to any authenticated session can enumerate the **entire authorization model** of the application.

- **PoC (Proof of Concept) Attack Vector:**
  ```
  1. Authenticate as any user (e.g., demo/1234)
  2. Navigate to http://localhost:8080/main
  3. Observe the full role enumeration table
  4. Identify all available scopes and actions
  5. Use this information to craft targeted attacks against specific routes
  ```

- **Remediation:**
  1. Remove the role enumeration table from the main page.
  2. Display only user-friendly information (name, last login).
  3. Remove the `UHasRole('customers', 'xxx')` test — it serves no purpose other than exposing the API.
  4. Consider removing the `{{ cRoles }}` display entirely.

