### L2 — External CDN Dependencies Without Subresource Integrity

- **Vulnerability Name & CWE ID:** Supply Chain Attack / Integrity Violation — CWE-829
- **Severity Rating:** 🟢 **Low**
- **Technical Explanation:**  
  The application loads Bootstrap 5.3.3 and Bootstrap Icons 1.11.3 from `cdn.jsdelivr.net` without Subresource Integrity (SRI) hashes:
  ```html
  <!-- www/views/common/header.html -->
  <link href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@5.3.3/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css" rel="stylesheet">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap-icons@1.11.3/font/bootstrap-icons.min.css">
  <script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@5.3.3/dist/js/bootstrap.bundle.min.js"></script>
  ```

  If the CDN is compromised (or an attacker performs a DNS poisoning/MITM attack), malicious code could be injected into every page that loads these resources. No `integrity` or `crossorigin` attributes are present.

- **PoC (Proof of Concept) Attack Vector:**
  ```
  1. Perform DNS spoofing or MITM on the network path to cdn.jsdelivr.net
  2. Serve a modified bootstrap.bundle.min.js containing malicious JavaScript
  3. All users loading the application execute the attacker's code
  4. Potential for session hijacking, credential theft, or defacement
  ```

- **Remediation:**
  1. Add SRI hashes to all external resources:
     ```html
     <link href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@5.3.3/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css"
           rel="stylesheet"
           integrity="sha384-SL..."
           crossorigin="anonymous">
     <script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@5.3.3/dist/js/bootstrap.bundle.min.js"
             integrity="sha384-..."
             crossorigin="anonymous">
     </script>
     ```
  2. Consider self-hosting critical frontend dependencies.
  3. Implement a Content-Security-Policy that restricts script sources.

